flowchart LR
    Patch["<b>1. patched function entry</b><br/>architecture ftrace/BPF machinery turns NOP space into an entry call path<br/><b>handoff:</b> trampoline must run before the function body<br/><b>state:</b> original arguments are still available"]

    Tramp["<b>2. BPF trampoline</b><br/>saves argument registers and builds the BPF calling convention<br/><b>handoff:</b> verifier-approved program expects typed args/ctx<br/><b>state:</b> BPF-visible arguments are ready"]

    Prog["<b>3. fentry program</b><br/>observes filename_unlinkat arguments before unlink logic runs<br/><b>handoff:</b> return 0 continues kernel execution<br/><b>state:</b> optional event data is prepared"]

    Event["<b>4. tracing side effect</b><br/>ringbuf or map update exposes observation to userspace<br/><b>handoff:</b> trampoline can restore normal execution<br/><b>state:</b> event is recorded without changing syscall behavior"]

    Body["<b>5. original function body</b><br/>registers restored, filename_unlinkat performs lookup, permission checks, unlink<br/><b>state:</b> caller sees the normal kernel return value"]

    Patch --> Tramp --> Prog --> Event --> Body

    classDef hot fill:#ffe5b4,stroke:#d97706,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bpf fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb,stroke-width:2px
    classDef kern fill:#e5e7eb,stroke:#374151,stroke-width:2px
    class Patch,Tramp hot
    class Prog,Event bpf
    class Body kern
